            <h1>closely colocated words</h1>
<p>words that appear almost exclusively within a single phrase</p>
<ul>
<li>(disgruntled) employees</li>
<li>(unbridled) rage</li>
</ul>
<h1>usually prefixed word roots</h1>
<p>words that almost always are used with some prefix (usually negation), even though the base is also a word.</p>
<ul>
<li>(dis)gruntled</li>
<li>(dis)appointed</li>
<li>(im)mediately</li>
<li>(un)ravel - oddly enough, ravel and unravel are synonyms</li>
</ul>

